.TH XTHREAD 3 "2026-10-15" "xthread" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
xthread \- cross-platform thread and mutex utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <xthread.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef " "platform-specific-type" " xmutex_t;"
.PP
.BI "int xmutex_init(xmutex_t *" m ");"
.BI "void xmutex_lock(xmutex_t *" m ");"
.BI "void xmutex_unlock(xmutex_t *" m ");"
.BI "void xmutex_destroy(xmutex_t *" m ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B xthread
library provides a cross-platform mutex interface for synchronizing access to shared resources.
.PP
On Windows, the implementation uses Windows Critical Sections
.RB ( CRITICAL_SECTION ).
On POSIX-compatible systems, it uses POSIX Threads
.RB ( pthread_mutex_t ).
.SH TYPES
.TP
.B xmutex_t
The platform-specific mutex type selected by the header.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BI "int xmutex_init(xmutex_t *" m );
Initializes the mutex pointed to by
.IR m .
Returns zero on success. On POSIX systems, a nonzero error code indicates failure.
.TP
.BI "void xmutex_lock(xmutex_t *" m );
Locks the initialized mutex. The calling thread blocks until the mutex can be acquired.
.TP
.BI "void xmutex_unlock(xmutex_t *" m );
Unlocks a mutex previously acquired by the calling thread.
.TP
.BI "void xmutex_destroy(xmutex_t *" m );
Destroys the mutex and releases its associated resources. The mutex must not be locked or in use by another thread.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <xthread.h>

int main(void)
{
    xmutex_t mutex;

    if (xmutex_init(&mutex) != 0)
        return 1;

    xmutex_lock(&mutex);
    /* Access shared resources here. */
    xmutex_unlock(&mutex);

    xmutex_destroy(&mutex);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B xmutex_init
returns zero on success and a nonzero error code on POSIX initialization failure. The remaining functions return no value.
.SH NOTES
The mutex must be initialized before use. Only its owning thread should unlock it. Destroying a locked mutex or one still in use by another thread is invalid.
.PP
POSIX builds may require linking with the platform's thread library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pthread_mutex_init (3),
.BR pthread_mutex_lock (3),
.BR pthread_mutex_unlock (3),
.BR pthread_mutex_destroy (3)
